    "proposition_id": "GDiSSmcZ89HD",
    "text": "The electron gyromagnetic ratio can be related to the electron's magnetic moment and its mass as follows: |\u0263e| = \u03bce / (I \u00b7 e) and \u03bce = gLe\u03bcB, where gL = 2 (Lorentz factor for the electron), e is the electron charge, I = \u210f / (2m_e) is the electron's intrinsic angular momentum, m_e is the electron mass, and \u210f is the reduced Planck constant",
    "source_node": "sd6E",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
